==Strategy==
This fight will not be very difficult, at least until the last phase.

Essentially, you want to fight all 3 Z-Onel waves separately by luring and killing. In the first two waves, Z-Onel is supported by weak peons, making her easy to kill. Do keep in mind that although she is the main threat, she is not spawned as the boss, making her susceptible to being knocked behind the enemy base, which can be a major problem in the next phase.

Avoid spawning too many units so that the dark doges can still kill the stack and allow Z-Onel to be lured back away from the enemy base. Otherwise it is very likely that within the 4 KBs, Z-Onel will reach the enemy base and trigger the next wave.

The most difficult phase (regardless of how many Z-Onels you left alive) will inevitably be the third phase, where you will fight a St. Dober and Chibinel along with a squad of Gabriels. St. Dober must be crowd-controlled to prevent him from setting off [[Surge Attack|Surges]], meaning that meatshielding will be a liability unless you paralyse him with freeze.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Shigong Cat]]: This is the easiest Z-killer to use since it requires no timing due to its resistance to zombie. After fighting off the initial peons, simply send a stream of them into the blind-spot.
*[[Ancient Egg: N110 (Rare Cat)|Farmboy Cat]]: Sporting high range, high attack rate and a high slow chance, this unit is very potent when it comes to slowing down St. Dober. Single Target hardly ever matters because peons don't come out frequently.
*[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]]: Spammability, high speed and high [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel]] DPS allow this unit to tear through St. Dober and reach into the blind spot of Chibinel, but beware of his low range.
*[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]: Has lower DPS and a longer cooldown compared to Cafeteria, but has higher range and is generally more accessible.
*[[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Catcrates]]: With a fast attack rate, good DPS and an emergency Conjure, this unit can easily freeze all the [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] in this stage, but do note he is rather pricey and has a long cooldown, meaning you must make him count when you send him. However, [[Adherence to Virtue|the stage that he comes from]] is rather late game.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]]: When given the Massive Damage and Attack Buff [[Talents]] (and ideally HP Buff), Heavy Assault C.A.T. can serve as a rusher for the Doge Dark and Shadow Boxer K that appear in the second wave. Their high speed makes them significantly less vulnerable to being hit by Z-Onel than other options such as [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] or [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Assassin BearCat]].
*Pizza Cat: With massive damage against [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark Enemies]], he may pick off Doge Darks and especially Shadow Boxer K, but is otherwise bad versus Z-Onel due to his slow speed. He can still tank a few hits and survive, if boosted well enough.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: With insanely high speed and DPS (especially after maxing his [[Explosion]] Talent), he's very, very effective when it comes to beating up St. Dober whilst also being able to reach into Z-Onel's blind spot.
*[[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]]: The least consistent of all anti-Angel crowd-controllers mentioned, but he is the most accessible, as Farmboy costs Blue Behemoth Gems and Soractes is unlocked from a [[Adherence to Virtue|stage very late into the game]]. He has an unreliable chance to slow, but if luck falls into your favor, he can still make a contribution by slowing down St. Dober.
*[[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Island Cat]]: Brainwashed Island is very effective for killing Z-Onel when she's alone, as once a Brainwashed Island gets in her blind spot, they'll start to curse her, making it easier for more and more Brainwashed Islands to get in too. As long as other attackers are used to take care of the peons, Z-Onel will be killed easily.
*[[Eggy Cat (Rare Cat)|Easter Egg Cat]]: Due to its 100% proc and 100% uptime on slowing angels, Easter Egg Cat is really helpful on helping your Sanzo or Farmboy proc without relying on RNG, especially when you are using holy blast. It can also work on its own, but do note that its uptime barely reached 100% and it can screw you up after St. Dober's 1st knockback.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kalisa]]: High speed, anti-Angel DPS and good range enables her to be effective versus St. Dober.
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru]]: With high speed, anti-Angel Damage and Surge Immunity, if you're able to abuse his multiple rebounds, you can get insanely high damage on St. Dober.
*[[Ushiwakamaru (Legend Rare Cat)|Colossal Benkei]]: Colossal Benkei destroys St. Dober and is tanky enough to not take serious damage from his Surges. If you happen to own this unit, it makes the stage practically free. Do be warned that you must lure St. Dober or else this won't work.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]]/Jizo's Mega Castle: In his first form, he acts similarly to Pizza Cat and Mushroom Cat with a low cooldown and great DPS against Angel and Dark enemies, often saving slots. In his True Form, he acts similar to Benkei in which he deals insanely high damage per hit from a much higher range compared to Benkei.
*[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]]: Thunder Jack makes the last wave a piece of cake thanks to his high speed and great chance to knockback Angels. With good luck, St. Dober will be completely unable to push forward and land a Surge, but he may also cause the Great Angel Chibinel to stick around longer.

